{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387635-promissory-pacts","id":387635,"title":"Promissory Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-31T14:55:20-08:00","id":387635,"title":"Promissory Pacts","content":"Hello. Could someone help me understand promissory pacts from the Interface book please. The example I was shown makes little sense to me.<br /> <br /> From my reading of it, you can apply conditional triggers and cut-off points to either side of the pact but rather than it providing a discount to the affected side, it makes that side of the pact worth more. Is this right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4885-one-hundred-eyes","name":"One Hundred Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T08:56:22-08:00","id":388480,"title":"","content":"There is no &quot;discount to the affected side.&quot; There never has been for Demons. Everything is always added (never subtracted) to one side or the other. So, yes, it makes that side of the pact &quot;worth more.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or both sides at once, effectively zeroing each other out. But never subtract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:26:18-08:00","id":388723,"title":"","content":"Okay perhaps discount was the wrong word, how about &quot;makes it cost less&quot; such as bargaining for Damaged Goods as covered in the Bargains Great and Small section of Flowers of Hell.<br /> <br /> My main point of confusion still stands. Whilst promissory pacts are a useful tool to have at your disposal, why should adding restrictions and conditions make it cost more. Why should &quot;vast wealth&quot; for instance be of greater contractual value to the recipient than &quot;vast wealth upon the death of your parents?&quot; What was the written intention of these rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4885-one-hundred-eyes","name":"One Hundred Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:29:29-08:00","id":388829,"title":"","content":"Why should a longer duration cost more for the demon, when the mortal is getting life long skills and money and good looks? <br /> <br /> Upon the death of the parents might include avoiding awkward questions or guarantee you get the inheritance instead of your hated step-sister. <br /> <br /> A big part of it, IMHO, is giving you a level of control that normal pacts won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:10:06-08:00","id":388907,"title":"","content":"Ah! So the cost of adding conditional triggers adds to the demons side of the equation, regardless of which side is actually affected by the condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4885-one-hundred-eyes","name":"One Hundred Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:59:03-08:00","id":388974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Hundred Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387635-promissory-pacts?p=388907#post388907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah! So the cost of adding conditional triggers adds to the demons side of the equation, regardless of which side is actually affected by the condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. A promissory delay is effectively an extension of the duration beyond the base value. Using them to set up cults and Covers months in advance is of greater use than having to manage the balancing act of a spare identity before you strictly need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T16:31:38-08:00","id":389099,"title":"","content":"You say no when I suggest the cost of the delay always applies to the demons side but then go on to say that it acts as an extension to the duration, but the duration is always factored on the demon's side of the pact so I really don't follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so 2 pacts that use the Specific Date (+1) delay.<br /> <br /> Example 1: The human gets lots of money starting from next year and in return the demon gets the human's dog immediately.<br /> <br /> Example 2: The human gets lots of money immediately and in return the demon gets the human's dog starting from next year.<br /> <br /> Most of the pact is shown below but in each example, which side gets the +1 for the specific date aspect? The side of the pact it affects, the side it doesn't delay, or the demon making the contract?<br /> <br /> Human: Greater Asset - Lots of Money (+3)<br /> Demon: Lesser Cover - Dog (+1), Duration - Permanent (+3)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4885-one-hundred-eyes","name":"One Hundred Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T16:44:31-08:00","id":389110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Hundred Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387635-promissory-pacts?p=389099#post389099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the duration is always factored on the demon's side of the pact</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The example in the Promissory Pacts section puts the lie to this immediately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Duration,&quot; DtD Core p193</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The duration on the demon\u2019s side of the pact need not match a person\u2019s. It is all too easy to convince a chronic gambler to gain fantastic wealth for one day in exchange for giving up his wife for a year \u2026 or forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The example in the corebook is knackered. The demon gets the Specific Date delay in your second example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:07:29-08:00","id":389135,"title":"","content":"Ah right! Those examples were really throwing me. So the now horribly unbalanced first example it would look like this?<br /> <br /> &quot;The human gets lots of money starting from next year and in return the demon gets the human's dog immediately.&quot;<br /> Human: Greater Asset - Lots of Money (+3), Duration - Permanent (+3), Specified Date - Starts New Years Day (+1)<br /> Demon: Lesser Cover - Dog (+1), Duration - Permanent (+3)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4885-one-hundred-eyes","name":"One Hundred Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}